# Whether every member of a ball with a one-limb center is positive, and the ball is not empty
# (milestone2.md, "One enclosure interface", the row of certainly_positive()): c - r > 0, decided
# exactly as r < c. False for the empty set (a NaN compares false) and for the whole line (+inf < 0
# is false). The comparison of Ball<T, 1>::certainly_positive, written by hand in
# include/kairn/ball.hpp. Exact.
kernel:        ball_positive_1
input:         stored c
input:         stored r
output:        mask m
requires:      ball c r
ensures:       certain m lt 0 x x=c,r exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the radius compared with the center (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBallPredicates.v ball_positive_1_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the results are masks, which have no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical ball

m = lt(r, c)
